Z||000000||fieroburton||08-03-2001||01:55 PM||||my left dash speaker went out when I replaced the speaker, so I got some radio wire and ran a wire from the right dash speaker to the left .<BR>will this hurt my radio ?<P>------------------<BR>1984 2M4 SE <BR>    <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||JamesWM83||08-03-2001||02:26 PM||||No.. it won't hurt anything but sound. Radio's are set up with a left and right channel for a reason. Each channel picks up different parts of the music. But both will pick up some of everything. It won't hurt anything... just it will lack the sound quality it had before. LAtes<P>------------------<BR>~JAmes||||reg||1
Z||000002||Posthumane||08-03-2001||02:48 PM||||You basically have mono sound from the right channel only. It's not the best solution, but i know what a pain in the @$$ it is to run new wire under the dash from the radio. Yo basically have to rip apart your whole front end interior.||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnF||08-03-2001||03:24 PM||||Mono sound from front & stero in the rear isn't the best.  New wiring is difficult.  Simply put speakers in both doors.  Easier and simpler.||||reg||3
